; -*- mode: lisp -*-
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; AUTHORED. See weave4.task for the shared design -- the spool fixture, the seat
; geometry and the 8.25 mm it is pinned to, the worst_of grouping and the zero
; idle floor -- and difficulty.py for what a LEVEL is.
;
; A DRAWN BOARD BESIDE weave4. This is weave4's station count, rod and seats with
; the stations UN-FIXED: a layout drawn fresh for every episode instead of
; written down.
;
; WHAT VARIES, per episode: the gap between each adjacent pair of stations, how
; far each station is staggered off the line, a small wander on top of that, the
; whole board's rotation, and where its centroid sits. Five things, none of them
; the same twice, and the rod's own bow drawn beside them. What does NOT vary is
; the station count -- this document declares four fixtures and four seats,
; and a board with a different number of stations is a different document.
;
; WHY THIS IS A SAMPLE AND NOT A JITTER. Every draw is measured before it is
; accepted: its accumulated turning angle has to land between 50 and 81 degrees,
; which is L1's band with ten per cent of margin at each edge; every station has
; to be wrapped by at least 9 degrees, so no board is quietly a row of stations
; the route walks past; no two seats may overlap; every station has to be inside
; the working arm's measured envelope; and the route has to fit the rod with the
; family's 20 mm of slack to spare. A draw that misses any of them is thrown
; away and another is taken. See WEAVE_BOARD in staging.py.
;
; That is the difference this variant exists to make. weave4 is ONE board and a
; score on it is a score on that board -- its spacing, its particular reach,
; whichever of its crossings happens to be the awkward one. A score here is a
; score on the LEVEL, because the level is what the boards are drawn from and
; the only thing eight of them have in common.
;
; The fixed rung stays, and both are wanted. A regression needs a layout that
; does not move; a generalisation claim needs one that does.
;
; WHAT THE `_l2` IN THE NAME IS. The LADDER RUNG this is drawn beside, not the
; band it lands in -- and at the shipped 155 mm pitch those stopped being the
; same number. weave4's declared board measures 36.5 degrees, which is L1, so
; that is the band drawn here. The sampler reads the level off the declared
; layout rather than off this document's name, so the two cannot disagree; the
; name is what a reader of the ladder expects and difficulty.py is what says
; which band it is. Nothing in the suite reaches L4 at this pitch.
;
; A DRAWN BOARD IS TIGHTER THAN THE FIXED ONE IT IS DRAWN BESIDE. The stations
; go down on a 72 to 92 mm pitch against the fixed layouts' 155, because as many
; as six of them have to fit inside the arm's measured band. What is held constant across
; the two is the TURNING, which is the axis a level is a band in, and not the
; spacing.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(define (problem DRAW_AND_WEAVE_A_FOUR_STATION_BOARD)

  (:suite cable_route)

  (:language weave the cable between the four pegs, alternating sides)

  (:staging
    (:cameras cable_board_l2@v1)
    ; The board sampler, registered by this task beside its own documents
    ; because every rule it draws under -- the reach band, the seat pitch, the
    ; rod's length, the level -- is this suite's rather than the library's. It
    ; emits the stations AND the rod's bow, and both change the model, so every
    ; episode is a rebuild rather than a re-pose.
    (:episodes (:count 8) (:seed 0) (:sampler staging:WEAVE_BOARD))
    ; weave4's budget. A drawn board is not systematically longer than the one
    ; it is drawn beside -- the turning is what is held constant, and the route
    ; length follows it.
    (:max-steps 6000)
  )

  ; weave4's rod: 0.80 m at 68 capsules. The DECLARED board below is
  ; weave4's own line, and it is what the scene builds when nothing samples --
  ; and, more to the point, what the sampler measures to find out which level it
  ; is drawing for.
  (:objects
    cable - board_l2_cable
  )

  (:fixtures
    peg0 - board_l2_peg0
    peg1 - board_l2_peg1
    peg2 - board_l2_peg2
    peg3 - board_l2_peg3
  )

  ; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  ; THE SEATS ARE weave4'S, UNCHANGED, and this is the document where that stops
  ; being tidiness and becomes the whole mechanism. A seat is a box in its own
  ; station's frame. The stations move every episode; the boxes move with them,
  ; and not one number below has to know where any of them went.
  ;
  ; That works because a region resolves against its frame's compiled pose
  ; rather than against a constant -- so a board the episode arranges is scored
  ; by the seats the episode arranged with it. A goal stated in world
  ; coordinates could not have this variant at all.
  (:regions
    (seat0 (:target peg0) (:ranges ((-0.045 -0.035 -0.003 0.035))))
    (seat1 (:target peg1) (:ranges (( 0.003 -0.035  0.045 0.035))))
    (seat2 (:target peg2) (:ranges ((-0.045 -0.035 -0.003 0.035))))
    (seat3 (:target peg3) (:ranges (( 0.003 -0.035  0.045 0.035))))
  )

  ; No init constraint: both arms at home, touching nothing. See weave4.
  (:init)

  ; 0.047 of this rod is about 3.2 of its 68 bodies -- weave4's own share,
  ; unchanged, because the rod is unchanged. See weave4 for what a share means
  ; and weave6 for why it moves when the capsule count does.
  (:goal
    (worst_of
      (And
        (>= (containment cable seat0) 0.047)
        (>= (containment cable seat1) 0.047)
        (>= (containment cable seat2) 0.047)
        (>= (containment cable seat3) 0.047)
      )
      (And
        (> (tcp-distance cable) 0.05)
        (<= (speed cable) 0.05)
      )
    )
  )

  (:observe
    (once (<= (tcp-distance cable) 0.05))
    (straightness cable)
  )

  ; The same motion three ways: a routine, the oracle graph, and the vision
  ; graph that runs the same crossing loop off the `cable` camera. See weave4.
  (:artifacts
    (:routine "routine:RoutineWeave")
    (:graph gt "graphs/weave")
    (:graph vision "graphs/weave_vision")
  )

  (:provenance
    (:tier authored)
    (:source "this stack -- weave4's level, drawn rather than written down")
    (:note "four F1 spools arranged per episode by staging:WEAVE_BOARD, rejection-sampled
            until the accumulated turning angle of the scored route lands in L1's band with
            ten per cent of margin -- 50 to 81 deg -- with every station wrapped by at least
            9 deg, no two seats overlapping, every station inside the reach band measured by
            rigs/weave_reach.py, and at least 20 mm of rod left over. Station spacing, stagger
            depth, per-station wander, board rotation and centroid are all drawn; the station
            count and the rod are weave4's. The declared layout is weave4's own line, measuring
            36.5 deg, and it is what the sampler reads the target level off -- so this
            document names no coordinates that the fixed rung does not already justify. No
            scripted routine of its own -- RoutineWeave reads the stations off the compiled
            scene rather than off the layout table, which is what lets it drive a board it has
            never seen.")
  )
)
